# Other programs' right-click entries — 7-Zip, Git, TortoiseSVN — hosted in the app's own menus,
# and the Context menu page that decides which entries, the app's own included, appear.
#
# A run gets the extensions from CannedShellMenuSource, not from this machine's registry, so what
# this proves is the hosting: the section is built where it belongs, for the selection or for the
# folder's empty space, in the tree too, and the Settings page lists the extensions behind a master
# switch with a box each. What it cannot prove is a real handler's own items — those need the real
# registry and real COM, on a machine that has them.

tree .
refresh
assert-count 8

# --- A selected file: 7-Zip's submenu, "Open with Code", TortoiseSVN, below the custom commands ---

select photo.jpg
menu files 01-menu-file
assert-menu-item 7-Zip
assert-menu-item Add to archive
assert-menu-item Open with Code
assert-menu-item TortoiseSVN
# still there: the app's own items are untouched by the section
assert-menu-item Properties

# --- Empty space: the folder's background. Git Bash Here belongs here; 7-Zip, which registers for
# items, does not. ---

deselect
menu background 02-menu-background
assert-menu-item Open Git Bash here
assert-no-menu-item 7-Zip

# --- The folder tree's node menu gets the same section ---

menu tree 03-menu-tree
assert-menu-item TortoiseSVN
assert-menu-item Open Git Bash here

# --- The page that decides which appear: the app's own entries on the left, extensions on the right ---

settings context-menu
shot 04-settings-context-menu
settings close

# --- The app's own entries can be unticked too. A whole group (Cut, Copy, Paste) goes, and the
# picture must show one separator where it was, not two; an entry in both menus goes from both. ---

hide-menu-item cut
hide-menu-item copy
hide-menu-item paste
hide-menu-item copy-path
select photo.jpg
menu files 05-menu-file-unticked
assert-no-menu-item Paste
assert-no-menu-item Cut
assert-no-menu-item Copy as path
assert-menu-item Copy name
assert-menu-item Rename
assert-menu-item 7-Zip

menu tree 06-menu-tree-unticked
assert-no-menu-item Copy as path
assert-menu-item Analyse disk usage

settings context-menu
shot 07-settings-context-menu-unticked
settings close

# --- And back: the next opening reads the setting again ---

show-menu-item cut
show-menu-item copy
show-menu-item paste
show-menu-item copy-path
menu files 08-menu-file-restored
assert-menu-item Paste
assert-menu-item Copy as path
assert-not-launched

# --- Arranged: 7-Zip placed beside Compress, the clipboard group moved below Rename. One layout
# serves both menus; the tree shows the same order without what it does not offer, and the
# extensions nobody placed still arrive at @more. ---

menu-layout app:new - app:open app:run-as-admin app:open-new-tab app:open-new-pane app:open-terminal app:open-vscode app:disk-usage app:duplicates app:changes app:compare-panes app:compress clsid:{23170F69-40C1-278A-1000-000100020000} app:extract - app:copy-path app:copy-name app:compare-files app:settle-by-content app:verify-checksums app:checksum - app:rename app:delete app:delete-permanently app:bookmark - app:cut app:copy app:paste @more - app:properties
select photo.jpg
menu files 09-menu-file-arranged
assert-menu-order Compress | 7-Zip | - | Copy as path | - | Rename | Bookmark | - | Cut | Paste | - | Open Git Bash here | TortoiseSVN | - | Properties

menu tree 10-menu-tree-arranged
assert-menu-order What changed here | 7-Zip | - | Copy as path | - | Delete | Bookmark | - | TortoiseSVN | - | Properties

# The page shows the arrangement, drags draw their line, and a new command lands under the
# selection with its editor open.
settings context-menu
shot 11-settings-context-menu-arranged
settings context-menu dragging
shot 12-settings-context-menu-dragging
settings context-menu new-command
shot 13-settings-context-menu-new-command
settings close

menu-layout default
menu files 14-menu-file-default
assert-menu-order Compress | - | Copy as path | - | Cut | Paste | - | Rename | Bookmark | - | Open Git Bash here | TortoiseSVN | - | Properties
assert-not-launched
